From aea116c4283f6b968573fb0853086cd65daec8b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:58:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lanes: a prompt can be read a chunk at a time, so other
 requests are admitted between its chunks (TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD=1)

A prompt's whole pass ran inside its admission (LaneHost.admitOne -> Engine.addStream -> Backend.prefill), so a request that
arrived while a long prompt was being read waited for the whole pass before its own began: a 250K-token cold prompt is two
minutes. PREFILL_INTERLEAVE_MS (0005) already ran decode rounds for the live streams between two chunks, but admission
still waited.

With TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD=1 the dsv41 backend offers prompt steps (Backend.VTable.prefill_step: one 2048-row chunk a call)
and the lane host reads its admitted prompts a chunk a turn, in turn, with the live streams' rounds (up to
PREFILL_INTERLEAVE_MS) between two chunks; a prompt that completes joins the rounds exactly as addStream leaves it
(Engine.fillStream). A short request that arrives during a long prompt is read after one chunk and decodes beside it.
Off (the default): the backend's vtable has no prefill_step and the whole-pass path is the code that ran before.

dsv41/lanes.zig: startFill is prefillFn's setup (slot, extent, placeParts/placeKept, the kept state's restore, fill_begin);
prefillStep is one iteration of its chunk loop plus its tail; selectFill returns to a prompt another prompt's chunk
interrupted with a new frame, fill_resume = 11 (slot, base: Model.fillBegin + Kv.fillBegin again on both ranks, which
also drops the Engram read-ahead that was staged for the other prompt). A prompt with pictures runs whole in its one
step (the model's image rows are a single set). Kv sharding: a half-filled stream is never moved or evicted by another
admit (parts.zig planRelocate takes decoding lives only), its twins may be revoked between chunks as before.
Both ranks must run the new image when the switch is on.

LaneHost: setup() (the lookup and stream build, split out of admitOne), fillOne(), occupied() and fillsPending();
deliver, takeCancels, failAll guard a job whose prompt is still being read; full_wait counts the prompts being read.
The prefill rate and seconds count a prompt's own chunks. Not with a trail (the arena a round resets holds its open
add event). The lone driver and the finish-near-the-end hold are not used in this mode.

Tests: lane_host_fill_test.zig (a late short request completes before a long prompt finishes, with the same tokens as solo;
cancel of either; a refused short request; a full pool retried with another filler); the host suites run a second time
with TF_TEST_PREFILL_STEPS=1 (resume, eviction, parked restores, deferred restores, pair break, stall monitor: all 94);
a stepped break during a prompt; the kind-11 assertion. The dsv41 step functions need a GPU and are not run here.

Design after the 4x recipe's 0031 (Mauvis Ledford; the loop's chunk rotation, Engine.fillStream, the fake chunked backend
and its tests), re-written for this tree's spill tier, parked requests, KV parts and pair-broken handling.
